t useful for forming pungs or chows and that are safe.\n\nReason: I choose to discard J1 because it is a single dragon with no immediate pairing potential, and there are still 3 unshown, making it relatively safe. Discarding it keeps my Bamboo tiles (T2, T3, T5) which might form a chow (T2, T3, T4 or T3, T4, T5) if I draw T4, or I could aim for a T5 pung. Also, keeping B7 pair is good for a potential pair or chow with B6/B8. Keeping F4 might pair with another F4 for seat/prevalent wind? F4 is North Wind, which is the prevailing wind, so a pung of F4 would give 2 points for Prevalent Wind. That's valuable. So I should keep F4. J3 is also a dragon, but less points. I'll discard J1 to reduce honors and keep F4 for potential wind pung.\n\nAnswer: Play J1"}
